    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Delightful four-bedroom, two reception semi-detached bungalow with well-maintained gardens front and rear presented to the open market ready for immediate occupancy. Ample car parking to the side with a cobble lock driveway and yard with a selection of block-built sheds to the rear. This home is vacant two years and may be subject to Vacant Property Grant. Nestled in a lovely mature development within stone's throw of Castlepollard town within easy access to all amenities both social and essential at your fingertips including TFI public transport.\n\nThe accommodation briefly comprises of the entrance hall with PVC door, Sitting room with front aspect and carpet flooring. A second living room with solid fuel fireplace and front aspect. The kitchen is to the rear with fitted with timber units. Ther are four bedrooms one to the front of the house all with carpet flooring and the family bathroom.\n\nThe exterior of this home is well presented with walled in front garden in lawn with some rose bushes, the rear garden is in lawn with block-built shed in three divisions and cobble lock driveway and rear yard.\n\nSuperbly located within minute's walking distance of Castlepollard town with its selection of local shops, Castlevaragh Hotel, pubs, Churches, Tesco shopping centre, doctor's surgery, post office, primary and secondary schools, sporting and leisure facilities including many lakes and rivers for water sport and fishing, Fore Abbey and Tullynally Castle and garden walks all to hand. Castlepollard is serviced with the New TFI Local Link 818 Mullingar to Castlepollard via Collinstown, offering 5 daily return services Monday to Thursday, 8 on Friday, 7 on Saturday and 5 on Sundays.\n\nViewing highly recommended.\n\nAccommodation\nEntrance Hall 1.603m x 0.928m (5'3\" x 3'1\"):\nPVC door.\n\nSitting Room 3.212m x 4.667m (10'6\" x 15'4\"): Front aspect, electric fire, carpet flooring.\n\nLiving Room 4.648m x 3.046m (15'3\" x 10'): Timber flooring, coving, ceiling rose, front aspect.\n\nBedroom One 3.691m x 2.542m (12'1\" x 8'4\"): Double room with front aspect, carpet flooring, built in wardrobe.\n\nKitchen 1.375m x 5.038m (4'6\" x 16'6\"): Gallery style kitchen with fitted timber units, tiled splashback, two windows rear aspect.\n\nBack Hall 7.574m x 0.789m (24'10\" x 2'7\"): Carpet flooring, two windows to side, walk in storage, back door.\n\nBedroom Two 2.295m x 2.316m (7'6\" x 7'7\"): Single room, rear aspect, carpet flooring.\n\nBathroom 1.663m x 2.522m (5'5\" x 8'3\"):\nFully tiled with WC, wash hand basin, shower cubicle with Mira unit, window, fan.\n\nBedroom Three 2.562m x 2.491m (8'5\" x 8'2\"):\nRear aspect, carpet flooring.\n\nBedroom Four 2.263m x 3.644m (7'5\" x 11'11\"): Double room with carpet flooring, rear aspect.\n\nSheds\nArea One 2.637m x 1.765m (8'8\" x 5'9\"):\nBoiler room, block built, concrete base.\n\nArea Two 2.785m x 2.427m (9'2\" x 8'): Concrete base.\n\nArea Three 2.785m x 1.446m (9'2\" x 4'9\"): Concrete base.\n\nSpecial Features & Services\n•Oil Fired Central Heating\n•PVC single glazed windows and doors\n•PVC Facia & Soffits\n•Outside tap\n•Mature shrubberies\n•Block built sheds with power supply\n•Private rear garden\n•Ample parking to the front\n•Extended c. 1980\n•Peaceful area\n•Stone's throw to Castlepollard town centre\n•Alarmed\n•Mains water\n•Mains drainage\n•Located close to primary school\n•Side entrance with cobble lock drive and rear yard\n•Ample car parking space\n•Built c.1958\n•Approx 99.09 (m2)\n•May be subject to Vacant Property Grant\n\nIncluded in Sale\n•Carpets\n•Curtains\n•Light fittings\n•Fridge\n•Washing machine\n•Fixtures & fittings\n\nBER Details\nBER Rating: G\nBER No. 119300176\n\nDirections\nEircode N91 TP48"
      },
